WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:02.627
So what's the difference between a teaching artist

2
00:00:02.627 --> 00:00:04.587
and a credentialed arts teacher?

3
00:00:04.587 --> 00:00:06.965
Both roles are essential
to arts education,

4
00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:08.758
but they're different
in some important ways,

5
00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:10.885
and knowing the distinction
will help you figure out

6
00:00:10.885 --> 00:00:11.970
which path is right for you.

7
00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.723
So a teaching artist
is a practicing artist

8
00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:17.475
who brings their craft
into educational settings

9
00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:19.394
like classrooms, after school programs,

10
00:00:19.394 --> 00:00:20.729
community organizations.

11
00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:22.313
It's flexible,

12
00:00:22.313 --> 00:00:23.732
it's usually project based,

13
00:00:23.732 --> 00:00:25.358
it's usually freelance.

14
00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.318
A credentialed arts teacher,
on the other hand,

15
00:00:27.318 --> 00:00:29.571
holds a state issued credential to teach

16
00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:31.948
in a public school - they're a classroom teacher.

17
00:00:31.948 --> 00:00:33.658
So this can be
a full time job

18
00:00:33.658 --> 00:00:35.577
with benefits
and union protections.

19
00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:37.203
Neither path is
better than the other,

20
00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.456
it just depends on
how you want to structure your career.

21
00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:40.999
Where you want your art to live,

22
00:00:40.999 --> 00:00:43.543
how much flexibility
or stability you want.

23
00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:45.795
You might start as a teaching artist

24
00:00:45.795 --> 00:00:47.338
and pursue a credential later,

25
00:00:47.338 --> 00:00:49.424
so pick the option that feels right for you

26
00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:51.843
and we'll help you figure out what fits.
